<title>INDONESIA: INDONESIA CENTRAL BANK MAINTAINS INTERVENTION BAND.</title>
<headline>INDONESIA CENTRAL BANK MAINTAINS INTERVENTION BAND.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Indonesia kept its dollar-rupiah intervention band unchanged on Wednesday at 2,378/2,682, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the market had speculated that the band would be widened or possibly removed altogether after the rupiah briefly tumbled to a historic low of 2,682 against the dollar before recovering on central bank intervention.</p>
<p>The market remained nervous as the rupiah was still under pressure from offshore, they added.</p>
